  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In March 2022, Brian Mazanec described AI as a critical technology with broad implications for DOD warfighting and business functions and said DOD was already leveraging AI. He cited current DOD uses of AI and machine learning for full-motion video, satellite imagery, and language processing, as well as AI-enabled intelligence applications in Ukraine. He said GAO found DOD's AI strategy lacked some characteristics of a comprehensive strategy and pointed to needed improvements in strategy, collaboration roles, AI inventory, and the AI Joint Common Foundation.",
   "sids": [
    "s2",
